# Sanctioned Unix-identity renumbers (one logical transition per line).
#
# Format (strict, whitespace-separated, exactly six fields):
#   <package> <kind> <name> <old-id> <new-id> <superseding-nvr>
# kind is `user` or `group`; ids are decimal; the nvr names the exact
# package revision whose declaration carries the new id.
#
# The history census (derive_ledger) stays fail-closed: any UID/GID
# change not matched EXACTLY here -- package, kind, name, old id,
# new id, and the introducing NVR -- still refuses. A consumed
# transition emits an audit notice. Malformed lines (wrong field
# count, unknown kind, non-numeric ids, duplicate keys, nvr not
# belonging to the named package) refuse at load, before any audit.
# Historical APKs are never rewritten; this file only lets the
# ledger REPRESENT a deliberate, reviewed renumber. There is no
# wildcard, no range, and no "any future renumber" form.
#
# polkitd 127 -> 156 (r2, 2026-10-14): UID/GID 127 senior-held by
# systemd-network (tombstoned since 261.2-r5); same deliberate act
# in both namespaces, one entry each.
polkit group polkitd 127 156 polkit-127-r2
polkit user polkitd 127 156 polkit-127-r2
